From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josip Seketa <josip.seketa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:39:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 52/76] gdb/remote: keep the selected thread when a thread list
 names a new process

A process first named by the thread list read at a stop left GDB with no thread selected (inferior_thread assertion).

diff --git a/gdb/remote.c b/gdb/remote.c
index db4bbb81597..49f3d1735eb 100644
--- a/gdb/remote.c
+++ b/gdb/remote.c
@@ -3291,12 +3291,15 @@ remote_target::remote_notice_new_inferior (ptid_t currthread,
 	{
 	  bool fake_pid_p = !m_features.remote_multi_process_p ();
 
+	  /* Leave the selected thread and inferior unchanged:
+	     remote_add_inferior switches to the new inferior, and so
+	     does fetching its target description.  */
+	  scoped_restore_current_thread restore_thread;
+
 	  inf = remote_add_inferior (fake_pid_p,
 				     currthread.pid (), -1, 1);
 
-	  /* Fetch the target description for this inferior.  Make sure to
-	     leave the currently selected inferior unchanged.  */
-	  scoped_restore_current_thread restore_thread;
+	  /* Fetch the target description for this inferior.  */
 	  switch_to_inferior_no_thread (inf);
 	  target_find_description ();
 	}
diff --git a/gdb/testsuite/gdb.replay/new-process-in-thread-list.exp b/gdb/testsuite/gdb.replay/new-process-in-thread-list.exp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..8b8243722cb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gdb/testsuite/gdb.replay/new-process-in-thread-list.exp
@@ -0,0 +1,171 @@
